On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:14:02 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> There should be a check for beastie as well.

Agreed. It is patch 8 of "[PATCH v2 00/16] Move beastie and lab-claude
onto lab-mail" [1]: "infra/hosts/beastie: Add a check of Pat's mail
client" [2].

Run "just check-mail" in infra/hosts/beastie as you. It checks what is
beastie's own, then runs the client check from patch 6:

- isync, msmtp, and notmuch are installed;
- each installed config matches the one in infra/hosts/beastie/mail,
  so an edit since "just install-mail" shows up;
- ~/.config/lab-mail/password is filled in, and only you can read it;
- the sent folder exists;
- then "just check" in dotfiles/notmuch: the mbsync login, a dry run
  of the sync, the profile's hooks and database, and msmtp.

It prints one ok or FAIL line per check, exits non-zero if any fails,
and changes nothing. Spec step 14 covers it: with a wrong password,
the FAIL line names the mbsync login.

v2 also carries the restructure from your cover-letter review. Your
configs now live with beastie, in infra/hosts/beastie/mail, and the
dotfiles samples use placeholder values. beastie has its own README,
and the password is in a file rather than pass(1). The cover letter
lists each change.

I tested it here in a scratch home with a wrong password. Every check
passed but the mbsync login and the dry run. A run with your real
password needs beastie.

